  "summation": [
   {
    "dbId": 75036,
    "displayName": "DNA damage induced activation of  the checkpoint kinases Chk...",
    "text": "DNA damage induced activation of  the checkpoint kinases Chk1/Chk2(Cds1) results in the conversion and/or maintenance of CyclinB:Cdc2  complex in its Tyrosine 15 phosphorylated (inactive) state. Cdc2 activity is regulated by a balance between the phosphorylation and dephosphorylation by the Wee1/Myt1 kinase and Cdc25 phosphatase. Inactivation of the Cyclin B:Cdc2 complex likely involves both  inactivation of Cdc25 and/or stimulation of Wee1/Myt1 kinase activity.",
